# Antigravity IDE Execution Rules

## 1. Automated Checks Restriction
- NEVER run automated TypeScript compiler checks (`tsc`, `npx tsc`, etc.) automatically after code modifications.
- NEVER invoke the browser subagent or capture screenshots for visual verification by default.
- Ignore project compilation errors during micro-tasks unless they directly block editing.

## 2. Testing Workflow
- Apply code changes and STOP immediately.
- Wait for explicit user validation.
- ONLY run `tsc`, linters, or the browser subagent when the user explicitly commands: "сделай полный тест", "запусти проверку" or "run full test".
